0\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MARCH 7, 2007\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Tamuri.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:31 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a), City of Calabasas v. RCS II Development Company, et al., BC 339068.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:30 p.m. from closed session and Mayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:40 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Rubin, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Tom Bartlett.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council accepted the settlement which was proposed in closed session. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r Mayor Washburn spoke regarding the election which occurred on March 6. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian announced an upcoming open house which will take place at the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center. Councilmember Wolfson commended staff on the successful election. Councilmember Maurer spoke regarding an upcoming Arbor Day Ceremony which will be taking place. Councilmember Groveman thanked everyone for the election and spoke regarding the low voter turnout of the election. Mayor Washburn spoke regarding the anniversary of the Malibou Lakes Club and spoke regarding the upcoming MethodFest Film Festival.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Ben Kalif, Uman Degoody and Tim Elkins, spoke in support of the proposed projects at 3460 and 3462 Lilac Trail, which are outlined in Items #6 and #7. Dale Reicheneder, Calabasas, representing the Steeplechase Homeowners Association, spoke in opposition to the Entrada at Malibu Canyon project, the Summit Development and stated that Steeplechase Homeowners Association would like to work with the City in developing a trail adjacent to its property. Norman and Michelle Dornfest, Calabasas, spoke in support of the proposed projects at 3460 and 3462 Lilac Trail. Gerald Smith, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the proposed project at 3460 and 3462 Lilac Trail. John Hodder, California Wetlands Research, spoke in opposition to the proposed project at 3460 and 3462 Lilac Trail.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the February 21, 2007 City Council meeting.\r \r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1064, seeking cost recovery for abatement of a public nuisance at 22439 DeKalb Drive.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1067, in support of AB 391, which enhances municipal membership on the South Coast Air Quality Management District (SCAQMD).\r\r Recommendation to accept completion of the traffic signal modification� project for the intersections of Park Granada at Parkway Calabasas and Agoura Road at Lost Hills Road; and to direct the City Clerk to file the notice of completion.\r\r Recommendation to approve the third amended employment agreement for the City Manager.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, 4 and 5. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\rThe following two public hearings were heard concurrently:\r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING: Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1057, to uphold the Planning Commission's decision to approve a request for a Conditional�Use Permit (File No. C.U.P.-004-018) and to construct a new single-family residence and 6-foot high retaining walls located at 3460 Lilac Trail (APN: 2072-011-006) within the Rural Community and Calabasas Highlands and Scenic Corridor Overlay Zone.\r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING: Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1058, to uphold the Planning Commission's decision a request for a Conditional�Use Permit (File No: C.U.P-005-010), and to construct a single-family residence 6-foot high retaining walls located at 3462 Lilac Trail (APN: 2072-011-007) within the Rural Community and Calabasas Highlands and Scenic Corridor Overlay Zone.\r\rCity Attorney Colantuono provided background information on the proceedings of the public hearing.\r\rThe City Council deliberated on the appeals.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to exclude the documents that were received after the deadline established by the City Attorney of March 2, 2007 at 12:00 p.m. MOTION CARRIED 4/1 with Councilmember Maurer voting NO.\r\rJohn Hodder, California Wetlands Research, provided further information in opposition to the proposed project. Robert Glushon, Luna & Glushon, and David Wolff, provided further information in support of proposed project.\r\rMayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve staff�s recommendation to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1057 and Resolution No. 2007-1058. MOTION CARRIED 3/2 with Mayor pro Tem Bozajian and Councilmember Maurer voting NO.\r\rThe City Council recessed at 9:35 p.m. and reconvened at 9:55 p.m.\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Recommendation to approve an agreement with EdgeSoft, Inc.�for the purchase and maintenance of a city-wide permit tracking system�for a 5-year period in the amount of $883,434.00.\r\rGeoff Starns, Senior Planner, presented the staff report.\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve the proposed agreement with EdgeSoft, Inc. MOTION CARRIED 4/1 with Councilmember Maurer voting NO.\r\r Recommendation from staff and the Civic Center Task Force to approve a negotiated amendment to the Civic Center construction contract with Bernards Bros. to a fixed value of $36,854,000.�\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve the negotiated amendment to the Civic Center construction contract with Bernards Bros. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of February 9, 2007 to February 23, 2007.\r\rNo Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson reported on the status of the Civic Center construction project.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that a phone survey will be conducted regarding the City�s updated General Plan. He spoke regarding a recent rate increase by Waste Management Services. \r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r Mayor pro Tem Bozajian requested to place an item on the April 4, 2007 agenda regarding forming a subcommittee to work with the United States Postal Service on postal issues in the City.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 10:25 p.m. in memory Lillian Martin, Greg Jordan, Camille Lia.\r\r\r\r______________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC\rAssistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r03/07/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00